      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CAPTAIN PAPRIKA (1) worked to find the lead and kept kicking only to find one better last time out over 2190m at this track. Likely to get all the favours from this nice draw. Big chance if anywhere near his best. LORD MYRMECIA (9) was out of the money two runs back at this track then displayed pleasing improvement last start to score by 1.75 metres over 1790m at the same circuit. Draws out a little on the second line and may need luck at some point. Perfectly placed and is sure to be there at the finish again. ACCELERE NZ (8) is a great chance after a string of sound recent performances, the latest a solid fourth at this track over 1790m. Hard to find fault. LESTER (5) is in the mix following a sixth at his first run back over 2100m at Charlton.",
